# Codex (OPUS-CODEX-20261005-01) on unit_named_struct_dead_tail_refused: Counter's written body reads g after a
# bare `return`, and g is Counter's input all the same (#dynamic).  Here the root gives g, declared above its
# call of Counter: the call is admitted, the tail does not run -- Counter\n stays 0 -- and the retained graph
# holds it: Counter, the unit's child 0, has five children, four without the tail.  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    return
    n: n + g
return
size_t: g 2U
Counter
int: ok 80
if: Counter\n = 0U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
